    "summary": "(Register 1971)\r\nWooden ceremonial trough with a horse&#039;s head and tail; on each side of the trough is a panel carved in relief with a lizard between eight pairs of human figures arranged in four columns, each with one pair of of figures standing upon another. The condition of the wood is both weathered and insect attacked, and had been subjected to a certain amount of primitive restoration on the part, presumably, of African dealers.",
